  "excerpt": "Perched on a remote ridgeline or tucked into the forest edge, The Offpost feels at home wherever the trail ends. Built for a traveling creative whose work moves between photography and film, this Mercedes Sprinter 170 AW",
  "body": [
    "Perched on a remote ridgeline or tucked into the forest edge, The Offpost feels at home wherever the trail ends. Built for a traveling creative whose work moves between photography and film, this Mercedes Sprinter 170 AWD is more than just a camper van. It’s a mobile studio, a quiet workspace, and a fully capable backcountry rig all in one. Powered by 800Ah of lithium batteries, 400 watts of solar, and a 3000 watt inverter, it keeps gear charged and creativity flowing without ever plugging in.",
    "Step inside and the atmosphere shifts. Rich Hinterland green cabinetry contrasts with the warmth of Castle Brown butcher block counters and a walnut acoustic slat ceiling. The dedicated workstation features a mounted monitor, blackout window shades, and thoughtful touches that make editing on the road feel effortless. Overhead strip lighting casts a soft, even glow across the cabin, while push-to-open latches and deep drawers keep equipment secure and out of sight.",
    "Outfitted for the wild, The Offpost rides on an Agile Off Road lift kit with all-terrain tires and Black Rhino wheels. A CA Tuned front bumper with a Warn winch stands ready for recovery, and an ARB air compressor, Diode lighting system, and full Owl Vans gear suite ensure nothing holds it back. From the Safari roof rack and XL Monster Box to the Starlink system mounted for remote uploads, every detail is built with purpose.",
    "Comfort is just as intentional. A tiled indoor shower, induction cooktop, Isotherm fridge, microwave, and queen memory foam bed make long days in the field feel a little more like home. Whether capturing sunrises in the desert or editing footage from a mountain trailhead, The Offpost is designed to meet the demands of work and the peace of solitude in equal measure."
  ],
